    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Over what period of time have you noticed these memory and attention problems getting worse? Did they start suddenly, or have they been gradually worsening over months or years?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it’s funny you ask it like that, whether it was sudden or gradual, because I can actually pinpoint it pretty much exactly. It’s been causing real, serious trouble for right about a year and two months now. I know the timeline so well because, well, that’s exactly when I had this big cardiac scare. You know, the heart thing I mentioned. \n\nMan, that was a whole ordeal. You go through life doing your thing, keeping busy, and then suddenly the doctors are telling you to pump the brakes, telling me I have to \"take it easy.\" Take it easy! I don't even know what that means! Before that happened, I was always on the move. I mean, I would be out walking for miles every single morning, just going and going, and then I’d spend the rest of the day deep into these big, heavy projects. Tearing down old sheds, building fences, hauling wood... whatever needed doing. \n\nAnd all that moving around, all that physical work... it used to keep me settled, you know? It burned off whatever it is inside me that keeps me going a mile a minute. But then, fourteen months ago, boom. The heart scare happens, and they forced me to completely cut back on the walking. I had to drop all the big projects. Suddenly I’m supposed to just sit around and rest? Me? Sitting still? It’s absolute torture. \n\nAnd I swear to you, Doc, ever since I had to stop doing the stuff that kept me grounded, that’s when my brain just completely unspooled. Without the walking and the work to keep me settled down, everything just scattered to the wind. So, yeah, a year and two months of this absolute nonsense.",
